{
 "name": "CRM · Deal stage changed → tasks",
 "nodes": [
  {
   "parameters": {
    "content": "## CRM · Deal stage changed -> tasks (Lesson 5.9)\nHubSpot Trigger on deal property change: dealstage. A Switch on the new stage creates the Card 4 tasks and notes. This workflow only creates tasks and notes and updates contacts; it NEVER changes the deal stage, so it can't trigger itself.\nOnly react to dealstage changes made by people: changes made by an integration are ignored.\n\nNo HubSpot Trigger on your setup (it needs a HubSpot developer app)? Use a 15-minute Schedule Trigger that searches deals modified in the last 15 minutes instead.\n\nCredentials: HubSpot Developer API (trigger); HubSpot App Token credential (the \"n8n Growth Desk\" private app token, with only contact, company and deal read/write scopes, plus tasks if you create tasks) (HTTP Requests); OpenAI; Telegram.\nPlaceholders: YOUR_STAGE_ID_TASTING_BOOKED, YOUR_STAGE_ID_PROPOSAL_SENT, YOUR_TOLU_OWNER_ID, YOUR_MODEL, YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID.\nRenamed default stages keep their internal IDs (for example qualifiedtobuy, presentationscheduled, closedwon, closedlost): check them in Settings -> Objects -> Deals -> Pipelines.",
    "height": 440,
    "width": 640
   },
   "id": "0d97ca62-b6d3-4060-8efa-de3f0056d485",
